    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance to help responders locate the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with posts or reflective delineators on both sides to make it visible at night or in low-visibility conditions.\n• Trim trees and shrubs along both sides of the driveway so emergency vehicles can travel its full length without obstruction.\n• Maintain a minimum vertical clearance along the driveway to allow ladder trucks and other tall emergency vehicles to pass without obstruction.\n• Create a turnaround area near the main residence so fire engines and other large vehicles can reverse direction without backing the full length of the driveway.\n• Keep the turnaround area clear of parked vehicles, equipment, and stored materials at all times.\n• Trim dense vegetation near the detached structure so responders can reach and move around all sides of it.\n• Keep a clear path between the main residence and the detached structure so responders can move between the two buildings on foot.\n• Post the property address visibly at both the road and near the main residence so responders can confirm they have reached the correct location.\n• Identify and communicate the single access point limitation to your local fire department so they can note it in pre-incident planning records."
