    "recommendations": "• Trim all shrubs that are directly touching or within a few feet of the house walls.\n• Remove brush concentrated near the base of the structure on all sides.\n• Thin scattered trees close to the house so their branches do not hang over the roof or walls.\n• Clear grass and low ground cover within the immediate area surrounding the structure.\n• Separate shrubs from each other near the house so fire cannot move easily from one plant to the next.\n• Remove dead or dry grass and brush from around any outbuildings or secondary structures on the property.\n• Cut back vegetation along the single access route so vehicles can pass through without obstruction.\n• Keep the driveway clear of overhanging branches that could block emergency vehicle access.\n• Thin brush concentrations visible in open terrain areas closest to the structure.\n• Remove grass and low brush from the edges of the driveway to reduce fire contact with the access route.\n• Clear a visible open area between the surrounding vegetation and the structure on all sides.\n• Keep scattered shrubs in open terrain areas near the house cut low to reduce the amount of material that can burn close to the structure."
